fstdumper Xcelium patch (wave-mcp)

Upstream : https://github.com/semify-eda/fstdumper
Base     : commit 3c7506333d2c9ad098d4526209621ea401a077ba
License  : GPL-3.0 (see docs/licenses/fstdumper-patches.NOTICE)
Apply    : bash deploy/build_fstdumper.sh <pristine checkout of the base>
           or: cd <checkout> && patch -p1 < fstdumper-xcelium.patch

Changes, all for Cadence Xcelium (Icarus builds keep upstream behaviour):
 * Scopes: interfaces; generate blocks, instance arrays, named begin/fork,
   static task/function locals and clocking blocks via vpiInternalScope.
 * Types: enum, packed struct/union, packed arrays, bit and integer nets,
   clocking-block signals.  Objects FST cannot hold (memories, strings,
   class handles, automatic variables, unpacked structs) are counted in one
   "FST info" line per $dumpvars instead of one warning per object.
 * Data: one declaration per signal; port-collapsed nets written as FST
   aliases (one callback per simulated net, FST_NO_ALIAS=1 disables);
   no-op value changes dropped; last changes before $finish flushed.
 * Names: RTL spelling for escaped identifiers and names containing '$',
   declared ranges such as [0:3] or [8:1], port directions, interface
   definition names.
 * Robustness: protected (encrypted) objects and objects without read
   access are skipped; NULL names, unusable sizes and over-long names no
   longer crash; named events no longer trigger VPI NOVALOB; one byte
   buffer overrun in show_this_item_x() fixed.

Files: src/sys_fst.c, src/vcd_priv.c (modified), src/fst_sv_vpi.h (new).

